--TEST--
a qualifier travels with a property the way it travels with a local, so `$this->token` off a `secret string` declaration carries `secret` at the access, and `self::$shared` does the same for the static spelling — the declarations themselves carry nothing, the word being written on those lines already, `rule:security/secret-qualifier`, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`, `rule:ide/semantic-tokens-carry-the-qualifiers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Handler {
    public secret string $token;
    public tainted string $body;
    public string $name;
    public static secret string $shared;
    public function reveal(): secret string {
        var $seen = $this->body;
        var $also = self::$shared;
        return $this->token;
    }
}
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens
--EXPECT--
2:7+7 class
3:26+6 property
4:27+5 property
5:19+5 property
6:33+7 property
7:21+6 method
8:13+5 variable tainted
8:21+5 variable
8:28+4 property tainted
9:13+5 variable secret
9:27+7 property secret
10:16+5 variable
10:23+5 property secret
